## 8. Content Gating (plan-based access control)

Gating is configured entirely through attributes and a data table field. No plan names or tier structures are hardcoded. Works with any Memberstack plan setup — tiered, per-course, or mixed.

### Setup

1. Add an `access_plans` field (or any name you choose) to the `courses` table in Memberstack.
2. For gated courses, paste the Memberstack plan IDs that grant access (comma-separated, e.g. `pln_abc123, pln_def456`).
3. Leave the field blank for courses open to all logged-in members.
4. Load `access-gate.js` before your page scripts (same as `MSDataCache`).

### Page wrapper attributes

| Element | Attribute | Value | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| Page wrapper | `ms-code-access-field` | `access_plans` | Name of the course data field that stores required plan IDs. Omit to disable gating. |
| Page wrapper | `ms-code-upgrade-url` | `/pricing` | URL for the upgrade CTA. Defaults to `/pricing` if omitted. |

### Locked state elements

| Element | Attribute | Value | Where |
|---|---|---|---|
| Locked overlay/block | `data-ms-code` | `locked` | Course detail page, lesson detail page. Hidden by default (`style="display:none"`). Shown when member lacks access. |
| Upgrade CTA link | `data-ms-code` | `upgrade-link` | Inside the locked block. Script auto-sets `href` to `ms-code-upgrade-url`. |
| Card lock indicator | `data-ms-code` | `card-locked` | Inside each course card template on saved-courses page. Shown per-card when that course is gated. |

### Course detail page (`/course`)

Add to the existing page wrapper:

| Element | Attribute | Value |
|---|---|---|
| Page wrapper | `ms-code-access-field` | `access_plans` |
| Page wrapper | `ms-code-upgrade-url` | `/pricing` |

Add a locked state block (hidden by default):

```html
<div data-ms-code="locked" style="display:none">
  <h2>This course requires a membership upgrade</h2>
  <p>Upgrade your plan to access this course and all its lessons.</p>
  <a href="/pricing" data-ms-code="upgrade-link" class="button">View plans</a>
</div>
```

When a member lacks access, the script still renders the course preview (title, description, cover image, category, order) but skips the curriculum, enrollment, and action buttons. The locked block is shown instead.

### Lesson detail page (`/lesson`)

Add to the existing page wrapper:

| Element | Attribute | Value |
|---|---|---|
| Page wrapper | `ms-code-access-field` | `access_plans` |
| Page wrapper | `ms-code-upgrade-url` | `/pricing` |

Add a locked state block (same pattern):

```html
<div data-ms-code="locked" style="display:none">
  <h2>This lesson is part of a gated course</h2>
  <a href="/pricing" data-ms-code="upgrade-link" class="button">Upgrade to access</a>
</div>
```

Lessons inherit their parent course's access requirement. The script checks the course's `access_plans` field, not the lesson's.

### Saved courses page (`/saved`)

Add to the existing page wrapper:

| Element | Attribute | Value |
|---|---|---|
| Page wrapper | `ms-code-access-field` | `access_plans` |
| Page wrapper | `ms-code-upgrade-url` | `/pricing` |

Inside the course card template, add a lock indicator (hidden by default):

```html
<div data-ms-code="card-locked" style="display:none">
  <span>Upgrade to access</span>
  <a href="#" data-ms-code="upgrade-link">View plans</a>
</div>
```

Members can still save gated courses (wishlist behavior). The card-locked element shows per-card when the member's plan doesn't match.

### How gating flows

- **No `ms-code-access-field` attribute** → gating is completely disabled, all content accessible.
- **Attribute present but course field is empty** → that specific course is open to all members.
- **Attribute present and course field has plan IDs** → only members with a matching `planConnection` see full content; others see the locked state.
- **`access-gate.js` not loaded** → gating is skipped silently; scripts render normally.

